I am trying to use pagedown::chrome_print() to pagenate HTML to an output pdf within RStudios. I wish to add page numbers in the bottom right corner page-margin box. I understand this should be applied under the page at-rule using margin at-rules . For example:

```
@page{
      size: 8.5in 11in;
      margin: 10%;
      @bottom-right-corner{
              content: counter(page);
      }
}
```

However, after some testing, I have not been able to apply any at-margin rules. However, other rules in the `@page` context are applied. In the example above, both size and margin percentage are applied to the page(s) when printed.

Attached is a simple HTML file (uploaded as a .txt file so GitHub will accept it) I have been using to test this. I have also tried applying a separate css file to this HTML file. The results are the same.

[simple.txt](https://github.com/rstudio/pagedown/files/11958965/simple.txt)

I am using pagedown 0.20, R 4.3.0, working within RStudios 2023.03.1 Build 446 and Google Chrome 114.0.5735.199

Hello,

There's an issue with text overflowing in both **\<code>** and also **\<div class="sourceCode r">** tags.

Here's the html_paged template with the following code just after the Introduction:
```
{r, echo=TRUE, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE}
print("WhenthePawnHitstheConflictsHeThinksLikeaKingWhatHeKnowsThrowstheBlowsWhenHeGoestotheFightandHe'llWintheWholeThing'ForeHeEnterstheRingThere'sNoBodytoBatterWhenYourMindIsYourMightSoWhenYouGoSolo,YouHoldYourOwnHandandRememberThatDepthIstheGreatestofHeightsandIfYouKnowWhereYouStand,ThenYouKnowWheretoLandandIfYouFallItWon'tMatter,CuzYou'llKnowThatYou'reRight")
```
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/79048392/191043409-32de9341-fb6a-4838-8818-a96e747a5367.png)

The fix is easy enough with a couple CSS tweaks:

```<style>
div.sourceCode {
  word-break: break-all;
}

code {
  word-break: break-all;
}
</style>
```

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/79048392/191045292-6a239322-cb17-425f-89e5-44ce78e4e412.png)


Could this tweak be added to the default CSS files?

Cheers!

Hi,

I'm opening this issue because I'm unable to modify the font size of footnotes in `pagedown` using CSS (MWE below). This problem seems to be present for other layout elements (eg, color). 

When I inspect the code of the footnote in the html output document, I always find `font-size: x-small;`, instead of the size I wanted. My best guess is that the Javascript treatment of footnotes in `hooks.js` (lines 294-308) is written in a way that cannot be overriden by CSS specifications.

Is there a simple solution I missed?

------

Here is a MWE:

**Rmd file**

```
---
title: "Test of footnotes"
author: "Daffy Duck"
output:
  pagedown::html_paged: 
    css:
      - style.css
paged-footnotes: true
---

# A first title
## A second title
This is an interesting text.^[This is a footnote.]
```

**Associated CSS `style.css` file**

```

h1  {
  font-size: 40px;
}
h2  {
  font-size: 30px;
}
body {
  font-size: 20px;
}
.footenotes {
  font-size: 30px !important;
  color: yellow !important;
}
.footenote {
  font-size: 20px !important;
  color: red !important;
}
span.footenote {
  font-size: 30px !important;
  color: blue !important;
}
```

